            <ArticleTitle>Comparison between MR imaging findings of intracranial and extracranial schwannomas.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>218-223</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0899-7071(17)30001-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clinimag.2017.01.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate the differences of MR imaging findings between intracranial and extracranial schwannomas.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We retrospectively reviewed the MR images of 98 schwannomas and compared the imaging findings between intracranial and extracranial schwannomas.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The number of intratumoral cysts was greater in intracranial than in extracranial schwannomas (4.8±7.2 vs 1.8±4.1; p&lt;0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The number of intratumoral cysts was different between intracranial and extracranial schwannomas.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
